# Milestone: M3
# Covers: 100k allocate-and-drop cycles complete within a bounded heap;
#         the GC reclaims dead cells and gc_live_bytes remains small relative
#         to gc_total_allocated.
#
# defer-to: M4 (object literals) + T28+ stress test in tests/stress/
#
# Reason: the {} object literal syntax used by the alloc-and-drop loop body
# does not exist until M4 (object model).  The equivalent C-level stress test
# (tests/stress/gc_long_running.c) exercises the same GC path at M3 via the
# urbi_gc_alloc / urbi_gc_slice / urbi_gc_force_full C API directly.
#
# When M4 lands and object literals are parseable, activate this fixture by
# uncommenting the urbiscript source below and removing this defer-to block.
# Expected behaviour: alloc_drop() completes without OOM; the runtime heap
# is bounded (live_bytes ≪ total_allocated at end of run).
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at M4):
#   function alloc_drop() {
#     var i = 0;
#     while (i < 100000) {
#       var x = {}|  x = nil;
#       i = i + 1
#     }
#   };
#   alloc_drop();
#   --- expected output ---
#   (no output — side-effect-free computation)
